  "id": "filter-theory",
  "term": "filter theory",
  "definition": "In this source, filter theory refers to a source-filter view of vocal production in which the sound made at the glottal source interacts with filtering processes in the vocal tract. The non-linear version emphasizes that source features such as pitch, loudness, and vibrato and filter features such as formants function together rather than independently.",
